  13 00207 2367         UNUSED  / Unused program area
  14            
  15            /
  16            / Line numbers are expressed in decimal, and stored as fixed point
  17            / in a single word.  The part to the left of the decimal point is 
  18            / multiplied by 128, and from 00 to 99 is added to represent the 
  19            / part to the right of the decimal point.
  20            /
  21            / The text strings end in '?M', the encoding for an ^M or carriage 
  22            / return.  The TEXT pseudo-op will generate a subsequent word of
  23            / 0000 for even length strings, which we elide with '*.-1' as 
  24            / necessary.
  25            /
  26            / The overall structure is a linked list of lines, where each 
  27            / line has a forward link, a line number, and some text.
  28            
  29                    DECIMAL
  30            L0P=0^128
  31            L1P=1^128
  32            L2P=2^128
  33            L3P=3^128
  34            L4P=4^128
  35            L5P=5^128
  36            
